    "run": "2026-09-30 fix run (review defects: irregular 860 x 770 top with black notches; light plate-top cap). Supersedes the first 2026-09-30 run (cut + cap at the rock section, cap baked from the Tripo plate top).",
    "top": "rectangular straight lip, UE 756 x 656 (task footprint, rim 50 uu around the ART-005 board: flat 46.5-47 + 3 uu bevel), 20 uu thick (Z -3..-23), ring solid with a 70 uu wide ring (inner opening UE 616 x 516, under the board frame). The board frame rests on the lip everywhere: no overhang over void, no notches in the top edge. The Tripo plate is not kept: it is 3-4 uu thin (reads as paper at the game camera) and its top texels are the light smooth lavender surface the review rejected",
    "body": "Tripo rock body cut at 2.5 % of the source height below its top, capped flat at Z -15 (inside the lip), section fitted inside the lip minus 6 uu per side with non-uniform XY limited to 5 % (4.76 %): UE 719 x 644; the long ends stay 18.5 uu further in. The body is recessed under the lip as in the concept; the deep notches of the rock section are under the lip, not in the top surface",
    "depth": "150 uu from the lip top to the lowest spike (unchanged): body Z scale 7.04",
    "lip_texture": "no new texture source: the lip strips and the hidden body cap are filled with the painted-rock texels of the Tripo skirt itself (texture bombing of 160 px rock windows, Hann blend with variance preservation, no mirroring), at the rock texel density (lip 1.32 px/uu vs rock 1.34); on the lip the low frequencies of BC are damped (box-blur 10 px x2: detail x1.3, low frequencies x0.4 - the painted crevice shading of the cliff read as cloudy blotches on a flat top) ; the tangent XY of the lip normals likewise (box-blur 5 px x2, low frequencies x0.3: the broad curvature of the cliff faces shaded as large dark blotches on the flat top) and BC x 0.5 (linear) so the lip reads as dark cracked stone and stays darker than the board in K1 (first try x0.85: rim 0.445 vs board 0.514 display luminance); normals copied in the strip UV frame (OpenGL, flipped to DirectX with the rest); AO baked over the whole tray. Rock texels unchanged (0 changed)",
    "uv": "lip = 4 unfolded strips (top -> bevel -> outer side -> bottom -> inner side, right-handed like the faces) in the atlas rectangle freed by the Tripo plate (px 16,16 1000 x 1068); body cap = small island (0.16 px/uu, hidden under the board). Rock UVs untouched",
